    "ssky_text_block_C9caN6": {
      "type": "ssky-text-block",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_44jwRr": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<p>History Books For School</p>",
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "center",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "heading_weight": "bold",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "center": false
          }
        },
        "text_6AiAPg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "max_width": 100,
            "custom_color": "",
            "alignment": "left",
            "text": "<p>Our books add depth and context to what children are already learning in school or through homeschooling. Instead of simply listing names and dates, they focus on big ideas like liberty, self-reliance, and the principles behind the founding of America.</p><p>They work especially well for homeschool families who want materials that align with principles like personal responsibility and individual freedom. With optional curriculum guides and audiobooks, it’s easy to build lessons around each chapter or just use them as a meaningful supplement.</p><p>If you're looking for history books that spark interest and encourage real thinking, our history books for kids are a smart place to start. We also offer<a href=\"https://tuttletwins.com/collections/books-for-teens\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">books for teens</span></a> that cover even more topics.</p>",
            "text_size": "regular",
            "text_weight": "regular"
          }
        },
        "button_4KBW6L": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "alignment": "left",
            "button_last": true,
